<!--
  DO NOT add SmoothPath: nav2's smoothers are NOT turning-radius aware and would
  produce undrivable paths. Smac's own radius-aware smooth_path:true handles
  smoothing. (item 89)

  Verified against the installed nav2 1.1.20: grepping both
  nav2_smoother/{simple,savitzky_golay}_smoother.hpp for
  `curvature|turning|radius` returns ZERO matches. A Savitzky-Golay filter has no
  kinematic model at all, so it will happily round a corner tighter than the
  1.00 m minimum turning radius this vehicle can actually drive.

  The absence of SmoothPath here is therefore DELIBERATE, not an oversight — the
  smoother_server block in nav2_amcl.yaml is dead config by design. What smooths
  the path today is the planner's own `smooth_path: true`, whose smoother IS
  radius-aware (nav2_smac_planner/smoother.hpp takes min_turning_radius).

  If path smoothing ever proves necessary beyond that, the turning-radius
  constraint must be re-imposed some other way — no stock nav2 smoother_server
  plugin will do it for you.
-->
<!--
  ===========================================================================
  REWRITTEN 2026-08-24 (CC_PROMPT_108). THE POLICY IS:
      AVOID   plan around the obstacle and keep going
      WAIT    only when no valid path exists at all, and STATIONARY
      NEVER   clear the LOCAL costmap while blocked.
      (A "NEVER reverse" rule was in force here from 2026-08-24 and was OVERTURNED
       on 2026-08-25 — the premise was wrong, see item 2 below. A bounded reverse
       now exists in the RoundRobin.)

  WHAT WAS REMOVED AND WHY. All four were actively defeating the avoidance the
  vehicle already does correctly:

  1. ClearEntireCostmap(local) in the FollowPath recovery. THE root cause of the
     infinite loop. It DELETED the person being avoided; the planner then routed
     straight through where they stood; the LiDAR re-marked them; the progress
     checker tripped; repeat. The recovery destroyed the evidence that avoidance
     depends on.

  2. BackUp, both occurrences (FollowPathRecovery and the RoundRobin). Measured
     2026-08-24: /cmd_vel carried 0.150 m/s negative, exactly backup_speed, so
     this was ALSO the reversing seen on 2026-08-23. behavior_server writes
     cmd_vel DIRECTLY, so MPPI's vx_min 0.0 and the DUBIN planner do not
     constrain it. Removing it is the only thing that does.
     ⚠️ PARTLY REVERSED 2026-08-25. The stated reason — "NO REAR SENSING" — was
     false: the Livox gives a full 360 deg scan with the rear sector 92.3% populated.
     ONE bounded BackUp is back in the RoundRobin (0.30 m at 0.10 m/s); the
     FollowPathRecovery occurrence stays removed. See the note at that node.

  3. DriveOnHeading 0.25 m. It drove AT the person.

  KEPT: Wait (stationary, forgets nothing) and the GLOBAL costmap clear. A stale
  global ghost is a real failure mode, and clearing it does not erase the live
  local obstacle.

  BOUNDED: a Timeout decorator wraps the navigate subtree. Nav2 registers NO
  wall-clock decorator (plugin_lib_names carries rate, distance, speed,
  goal_updated, single_trigger and path_longer_on_approach only), so this is
  BehaviorTree.CPP's OWN built in TimeoutNode: setRegistrationID("Timeout"),
  port "msec", registered automatically by the factory. A permanently blocked goal
  ABORTS instead of alternating forever.
  ⚠️ msec is 60000 (60 s), NOT the 300000 this paragraph originally specified. It was
  set to 300000 on 2026-08-24 to exceed the longest legitimate traverse of this map
  (31 x 39 m, 50 m diagonal, about 250 s at 0.2 m/s) and cut to 60000 the same day.
  60 s is therefore SHORTER than a full-diagonal traverse: a long leg can abort on
  time rather than on failure. Raise it if you route across the whole map.

  REPLAN RATE: raised 1.0 -> 5.0 Hz on 2026-08-24 (a person walks about 1.4 m/s, so
  at 1 Hz they moved 1.4 m between replans, wider than the vehicle; 5 Hz matched the
  local costmap's update_frequency), then RETURNED TO 1.0 Hz on 2026-08-26.
  ⚠️ The RateController below is hz="1.0". Note this no longer matches the costmaps,
  which both run at 5.0 in nav2_amcl.yaml — the moving-obstacle argument above still
  stands and is simply not being acted on at present.
  ===========================================================================
-->
<root main_tree_to_execute="MainTree">
  <BehaviorTree ID="MainTree">
    <Sequence name="NavigateWithClear">
      <!-- Once, at goal acceptance, NOT while blocked. Removes stale ghosts from
           a previous run before planning starts. -->
      <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearLocalCostmap-Start" service_name="local_costmap/clear_entirely_local_costmap"/>
      <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearGlobalCostmap-Start" service_name="global_costmap/clear_entirely_global_costmap"/>

      <Timeout msec="120000">
        <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="6" name="NavigateRecovery">

          <PipelineSequence name="NavigateWithReplanning">
            <RateController hz="1.0">
              <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="1" name="ComputePathToPose">
                <ComputePathToPose goal="{goal}" path="{path}" planner_id="GridBased"/>
                <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearGlobalCostmap-Context" service_name="global_costmap/clear_entirely_global_costmap"/>
              </RecoveryNode>
            </RateController>
            <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="1" name="FollowPath">
              <FollowPath path="{path}" controller_id="FollowPath"/>
              <!-- WAIT, STATIONARY. Was BackUp plus ClearEntireCostmap(local).
                   The vehicle holds position, keeps seeing the obstacle, and the
                   next replan arcs around it. It does not reverse and it does not
                   forget. -->
              <Wait wait_duration="1.0" name="WaitBlocked"/>
            </RecoveryNode>
          </PipelineSequence>

          <ReactiveFallback name="RecoveryFallback">
            <GoalUpdated/>
            <RoundRobin name="RecoveryActions">
              <!-- BackUp RESTORED 2026-08-25, bounded. It was removed because the vehicle was
                   believed to have NO REAR SENSING. That was later disproved: the Livox gives a
                   full 360 degree scan and the rear sector is 92.3 percent populated, so a
                   reverse is sensed, not blind. It was also removed under a never reverse
                   policy that no longer applies now the planner is Reeds Shepp.
                   WITHOUT this the tree has NO motion recovery at all: blocked by a person it
                   could only clear the costmap (which instantly re marks the person from the
                   live scan) and wait, forever. The operator saw the vehicle stop beside an
                   obstacle and do nothing, because there was nothing it was allowed to do.
                   Kept small on purpose: 0.30 m at 0.10 m/s. behavior_server writes cmd_vel
                   DIRECTLY, so neither MPPI vx_min nor the planner constrains it. The gamepad
                   remains the real stop at twist_mux priority 150. -->
              <BackUp backup_dist="0.30" backup_speed="0.10" time_allowance="10" name="BackOffFromBlockage"/>
              <!-- GLOBAL only. Clearing the LOCAL costmap here is what deleted the
                   obstacle and caused the loop. -->
              <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearGlobalCostmap-Subtree" service_name="global_costmap/clear_entirely_global_costmap"/>
              <Wait wait_duration="2.0" name="WaitRecovery"/>
            </RoundRobin>
          </ReactiveFallback>

        </RecoveryNode>
      </Timeout>
    </Sequence>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
